<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="csrf-token" content={get_csrf_token()} />
    <.live_title default="Mishka CMS" suffix={if(assigns[:admin_css], do: " - Mishka CMS")}>
      {assigns[:page_title]}
    </.live_title>
    {raw(MishkaInstaller.Event.Hook.call("RootHtml.MetaTags", %{html: "", assigns: assigns}).html)}
    <% css_href =
      assigns[:current_site] &&
        "/assets/css/#{assigns[:current_site][:name]}/#{MishkaCmsCore.Runtime.States.AssetsState.get!(assigns[:current_site][:name], "css")[:hash]}.css" %>
    <% js_src =
      assigns[:current_site] &&
        "/assets/js/#{assigns[:current_site][:name]}/#{MishkaCmsCore.Runtime.States.AssetsState.get!(assigns[:current_site][:name], "js")[:hash]}.js" %>
    <%!-- A SITE's stylesheet, for a site's pages. Not for the admin: the dashboard is not rendered
         with a site's components, so its bundle was megabytes of CSS the admin never used — and on a
         host whose site has never compiled, the href had an empty hash and 404ed. The canvas iframe
         is the exception and asks for it deliberately, because it must show the document exactly as
         production will; it takes the inline path instead, which is what `suppress_site_css` means. --%>
    <link
      :if={
        css_href && !assigns[:suppress_site_css] && !assigns[:admin_css] && assigns[:runtime_page]
      }
      rel="stylesheet"
      href={css_href}
      id="mishka-runtime-css"
    />
    <script :if={js_src} defer src={js_src}>
    </script>
    <script nonce={assigns[:csp_nonce]}>
      (() => {
        const setTheme = (theme) => {
          if (theme === "system") {
            localStorage.removeItem("phx:theme");
            document.documentElement.removeAttribute("data-theme");
          } else {
            localStorage.setItem("phx:theme", theme);
            document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", theme);
          }
        };
        if (!document.documentElement.hasAttribute("data-theme")) {
          setTheme(localStorage.getItem("phx:theme") || "system");
        }
        window.addEventListener("storage", (e) => e.key === "phx:theme" && setTheme(e.newValue || "system"));

        window.addEventListener("phx:set-theme", (e) => setTheme(e.target.dataset.phxTheme));
      })();
    </script>
    <%!-- The installer runs before any site, so no runtime CSS/JS bundle exists yet — load the
         prebuilt static LiveView client (`app.js`) directly for interactivity. The page styles itself
         with its own inline <style> (pure CSS, no Tailwind), so no stylesheet is needed here. --%>
    <script :if={assigns[:standalone_assets]} defer src={~p"/assets/js/app.js"}>
    </script>
    <%!-- THREE INDEPENDENT DECISIONS, three assigns. `full_tailwind` used to gate all of them at once,
         which is why the editor's canvas iframe downloaded the entire 2.5 MB admin stylesheet in order
         to get the two web fonts its inline `font:` shorthand names. The canvas renders a SITE's
         document and its own chrome is inline styles — it has no use for the dashboard's CSS.

         admin_css   → the dashboard, the builder shell, the login page
         admin_fonts → those, plus the canvas
         live_tailwind → the builder and the canvas only

         The admin chrome's own compiled stylesheet — see `admin_assets/admin.css` in mishka_cms_core.
         Its OWN file, touching neither of the other two CSS paths:

           * not `app.css`, because the runtime compiler inlines that into the static base and would
             then ship the whole dashboard inside every public site's stylesheet;
           * not the site bundle above, which is the site's own CSS and nothing to do with the admin.

         Before this the dashboard had no compiled CSS at all: every utility came from the browser
         JIT below, regenerated on every admin page from a 275 KB script. --%>
    <link :if={assigns[:admin_css]} rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/assets/css/admin.css"} />
    <%!-- Admin dashboard type system: Manrope (body), Space Grotesk (numerals/display), Newsreader
         (headings). Vendored rather than fetched from Google: their stylesheet redirects to fifteen
         `fonts.gstatic.com` files, so it was two DNS lookups and sixteen round trips before the admin
         could paint text. 624 KB in `priv/static/fonts/`, served with the app. --%>
    <link :if={assigns[:admin_fonts]} rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/fonts/fonts.css"} />
    <%!-- The same two faces for a DATABASE page, because that is what the seeded and starter
         designs are written in — `font-sans` and `font-display` in a site's `:theme` stylesheet name
         Manrope and Space Grotesk. Gated on `runtime_page` so the hand-written marketing pages,
         which bring their own type, render exactly the bytes they rendered before. --%>
    <link :if={assigns[:runtime_page]} rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/fonts/fonts.css"} />
    <%!-- THE GENERATOR, and only where a page cannot be styled ahead of time: the page builder and
         its canvas iframe. The reader types `px-7` into the inspector, or drops a kit component whose
         classes no build ever scanned, and the utility has to exist a frame later.

         Every other admin page is served by `admin.css` above. That was measured rather than assumed:
         the two heaviest admin pages were rendered, every class Tailwind generates for them was
         diffed against the compiled sheet, and the answer is now zero missing. The first attempt at
         this shipped 41 missing selectors and broke the dashboard — see `Mix.Tasks.AdminCss` for the
         two causes, both of which were invisible without that diff.

         Served locally, not from jsdelivr: measured cold the CDN answered in 780 ms, and it made
         drawing a page depend on the public internet. `mix assets.vendor` puts it in priv. --%>
    <%!-- A NONCE FOR A LIBRARY THAT HAS NO NONCE OPTION. The JIT below is Tailwind compiled for the
         browser; it delivers its output by creating ONE `<style>` element, which is exactly what
         `style-src-elem` governs, and it offers no way to mark that element as ours. Without this
         the editor would need `style-src 'unsafe-inline'` — which re-permits every injected
         `<style>` on the page to buy one legitimate element.

         So the element is marked on the way out: `createElement` stamps the nonce on any style it
         makes. Rules added afterwards are CSSOM writes on an already-allowed sheet and are not
         re-checked, so this one line covers every utility the editor will ever generate.

         It sits immediately above the JIT because it must be in place before that script runs, and
         it is gated the same way so no page that lacks the JIT carries the patch. --%>
    <%!-- THE SITE'S COMPILED CSS, ABOVE THE GENERATOR THAT HAS TO BEAT IT. It used to be rendered in
         the canvas LiveView's own markup, which is `<body>` — while the browser generator injects
         what it makes into `<head>`. Body comes after head, so the compiled bundle overruled every
         class the editor generated: an author typed `pl-[30px]` onto an element whose page already
         said `px-8`, the class landed, the rule was written, and the padding did not move.

         The bundle is base styling and belongs here; anything generated while the author works is
         appended after it and wins, which is the same order the published page has — there the
         override and the page's own classes come out of one Tailwind pass, correctly sorted.

         Linked and not inlined: a real site's bundle is megabytes, and it arrives compressed and
         cached `immutable` behind its content hash. --%>
    <link
      :for={href <- assigns[:canvas_css_hrefs] || []}
      rel="stylesheet"
      href={href}
    />
    <script :if={assigns[:live_tailwind] && assigns[:csp_nonce]} nonce={assigns[:csp_nonce]}>
      (() => {
        const nonce = document.currentScript.nonce;
        const make = document.createElement.bind(document);
        document.createElement = (tag, ...rest) => {
          const el = make(tag, ...rest);
          if (String(tag).toLowerCase() === "style") el.setAttribute("nonce", nonce);
          return el;
        };
      })();
    </script>
    <script :if={assigns[:live_tailwind]} src={~p"/assets/js/vendor/tailwind-browser.js"}>
    </script>

    <% js =
      MishkaInstaller.Event.Hook.call("RootHtml.InlineScript", %{js: nil, assigns: assigns}).js %>
    <script :if={!is_nil(js)} nonce={assigns[:csp_nonce]}>
      {raw(js)}
    </script>

    {raw(
      MishkaInstaller.Event.Hook.call("RootHtml.ExternalAssets", %{html: "", assigns: assigns}).html
    )}
  </head>
  <body>
    {@inner_content}
  </body>
</html>
